      "writtenOn": "2026-08-10T12:56:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t fully understand this change. org.freedesktop.systemd1.NoSuchUnit will only be returned when rsyslog.service is not present in systemd. Could you clarify the deployment scenario where rsyslog.service is expected to be absent? \n\nIf rsyslog is an optional component, should we explicitly validate the unit\u0027s existence before invoking ReloadUnit() rather than treating NoSuchUnit as a success path?",
      "revId": "370bc14dfef654d26b4e38c667110e6d55fc9e62",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62231cb8_f05709cf",
        "filename": "redfish-core/include/utils/eventlog_utils.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 468,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003017
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T10:56:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The intent here is to avoid returning InternalError for a valid ClearLog request on systems that do not provide rsyslog.service. In this flow, reloading rsyslog is only a backend follow-up step after the log content has already been cleared. If the unit is absent, there is nothing further for the client to correct, so treating NoSuchUnit as success keeps the Redfish action idempotent on a working system.\n\nI did consider checking for unit existence first, but that would add an extra D-Bus round-trip and still would not avoid races between the check and ReloadUnit(). Handling NoSuchUnit on the actual ReloadUnit call is the more robust path.",
      "parentUuid": "4465b7aa_ada4e8f8",
      "revId": "370bc14dfef654d26b4e38c667110e6d55fc9e62",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56c678dd_f8e6dccd",
        "filename": "redfish-core/include/utils/eventlog_utils.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 472,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-10T12:56:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not able to understand the reason for this change. Based on the Redfish specification, if the log file does not exist, the service should return a 404 Not Found response. In that case, returning a success message does not appear to be appropriate.",
      "revId": "370bc14dfef654d26b4e38c667110e6d55fc9e62",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "518c6425_ffa693be",
        "filename": "redfish-core/include/utils/eventlog_utils.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 472,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003017
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T10:56:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe the 404 interpretations does not apply here, because the Redfish action is defined on the LogService resource, not on an underlying filesystem object. ClearLog is specified as deleting all entries found in the LogEntryCollection for that service. If the collection is already empty, that is a valid no-op success rather than a missing-resource condition.",
      "parentUuid": "56c678dd_f8e6dccd",
      "revId": "370bc14dfef654d26b4e38c667110e6d55fc9e62",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d5fea5c5_9fe5b52c",
        "filename": "redfish-core/include/utils/eventlog_utils.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 472,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000153
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T16:40:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this case, the old behavior was correct.  If rsyslog isn\u0027t installed, but bmcweb is configured to use rsyslog, the config is broken, so internal error is appropriate.\n\n\nThere\u0027s no case where on an error we should return success as this code branch does.",
      "parentUuid": "518c6425_ffa693be",
      "revId": "370bc14dfef654d26b4e38c667110e6d55fc9e62",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
